  "set_up": "Pilatus 1M (981 x 1043 px of 172 um, the gaps of the public frame); direct beam uniform in the central 80 % of the detector; L uniform in 1.5-3 m; rot1, rot2 uniform in +-3 deg, rot3 = 0; lambda (0.5-2 A) chosen so that about 3, 4-6 or 7-9 rings lie on the detector (a third of the frames each); every order on the detector drawn as a Gaussian ring of 1.5-3 px sigma (2x2 sub-pixels; the public frame's rings are 5.5-6 px FWHM), first ring 2000-30000 counts, order^-(1.5-2.5), azimuthal modulation up to 30 %; background falling as 1/(1 + (r/r0)^2), r0 0.4-1 ring spacing, 1/10-1/60 of the first ring at its radius, plus 1-10 counts; Poisson counts; a beam stop of 8-20 px radius and its arm (1 % of the counts). Engine: standard agbh, energy and pixel size given, a distance estimate within +-15 %, tilt auto. 2theta of every sub-pixel from pyFAI's formula (detector_tilt.tilted_rays), not from lab_rays, which GIMaP fits with.",
